  "id": "DrugBank_DB00494 - MONDO_18466",
  "verbalization": "Entacapone is implicated in the pathogenesis of Hereditary Late Onset Parkinson Disease (HoPD) through a series of indirect pathways involving Cycrimine and Istradefylline. The evidence suggests that Entacapone may act as a precursor in the development of HoPD, as it is associated with both Early-onset Parkinsonism-intellectual Disability Syndrome and Hereditary Late Onset Parkinson Disease through shared indications with Cycrimine. Cycrimine, in turn, is linked to HoPD, indicating a potential role in the progression of the disease. The presence of Istradefylline as an indication for HoPD further suggests a possible downstream effect of Entacapone, though the exact mechanism remains unclear. The integration of these pathways highlights a possible link between Entacapone and HoPD, though the precise biological mechanisms underlying this relationship require further investigation.",
